SUMMARY:NASA Stories at the Ion: Building the Moon Base: Challenges and Opp
	ortunities at the Lunar South Pole
DTSTAMP:20260719T101343Z
DTSTART:20260730T083000Z
DESCRIPTION:Building the Moon Base: Challenges and Opportunities at the Lun
	ar South Pole \nIn this presentation\, Moon Base Principal Systems Enginee
	r Shatel Bhakta shares the many challenges NASA must overcome to realize a
	n enduring presence in the lunar South Pole region. He’ll also talk about 
	his journey at NASA\, the importance of human space exploration\, and what
	 NASA needs from the next generation of aerospace engineers. \nAbout the S
	peaker \nShatel Bhakta serves as the principal systems engineer for NASA’s
	 Moon Base. In that role\, he takes a system-of-systems view of Moon Base 
	infrastructure\, ensuring that all components work together to support NAS
	A’s goal of an enduring human presence in the lunar South Pole region. \nP
	rior to working on the Moon Base\, Bhakta served as NASA’s lunar architect
	ure lead\, guiding a multidisciplinary team across NASA centers to develop
	 a roadmap for crewed exploration of the Moon. This included developing as
	sociated conceptual reference missions\, concept of operations\, site plan
	ning guidance\, trades and analysis\, system element conceptualization\, a
	nd system-of-systems integration. \nBhakta earned his undergraduate degree
	 in mechanical engineering from The University of Texas at Austin and his 
	graduate degree in space architecture from the University of Houston. He i
	s a licensed professional engineer in the state of Texas. \n \n\nhttps://i
	ondistrict.com/event/nasa-stories-at-the-ion-building-the-moon-base-challe
	nges-and-opportunities-at-the-lunar-south-pole/\n\nFrom Ion District
URL:https://iondistrict.com/event/nasa-stories-at-the-ion-building-the-moon
	-base-challenges-and-opportunities-at-the-lunar-south-pole/
LOCATION:Ion – Forum Stairs\, 4201 Main St.\, Houston\, TX\, 77002\, United
	 States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:ion-district
CATEGORIES:Ion District
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
